# Claude Code machine-local settings — never publish (this repo is public)
.claude/settings.local.json

# Okular: only okularpartrc (durable preferences) is tracked. Guard against the
# rest ever being copied or --adopt'ed into the package, because `gpushall` runs
# `git add -A` and this remote is public:
#   okularrc  — window state plus a Recent Files list. Rewritten every session, so
#               it would churn a commit a day and collide on rebase between fedxps
#               and bigfed; it also names refereeing and teaching PDFs.
#   docdata/  — per-document bookmarks/annotations/page state, ~13MB and constantly
#               rewritten, mostly keyed to unsynced ~/Desktop/readings.
okular/okularrc
okular/docdata/

# --- Editor and OS scratch --------------------------------------------------
# Precedent, not hypothesis: `git add -A` has already published four of these —
# init.el~ (2025-10-30), sway/config.save (2025-11-09), and two nvim *.bak files
# (2026-03-19). Each was deleted later, but they remain in history.
#
# Two things sharpen this beyond the usual. Stow's default ignore list covers
# *~ but NOT *.bak/*.save, so an ad-hoc backup left in a package is symlinked
# into the live config tree as well as published. And ~/.bashrc.d,
# ~/.config/nvim/{lua,after}, and each ~/texmf/tex/latex/<pkg> are whole-
# DIRECTORY symlinks into this repo, so anything a tool writes under them lands
# straight in the working tree.
*~
*.bak
*.save
*.old
*.orig
*.rej
*.swp
*.swo
.*.sw?
.DS_Store

# --- Secrets: a second layer behind gpushall's vet --------------------------
# The vet (GSYNC_SECRET_GLOBS in bash/.bashrc.d/50-git-sync.sh) prompts y/N;
# these refuse outright. Kept deliberately in sync with that list, plus the
# names it does not carry. Note the vet fires only on paths NEW to the repo,
# so it cannot see a secret pasted into an already-tracked file — see TODO.md
# item 7. Anything here can still be committed on purpose with `git add -f`.
.env
.env.*
*.env
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
*.kdbx
*.jks
*.gpg
*.asc
*.ovpn
*.kubeconfig
.netrc
.npmrc
.pypirc
id_rsa*
id_ed25519*
id_ecdsa*
id_dsa*
known_hosts
authorized_keys
*credentials*
*_token*

# --- Build and tool artifacts -----------------------------------------------
# latex/ is a live stow package, and tests/nvim-syntax/run.sh is the one test
# that cd's into the repo (it opens tests/nvim-syntax/test.tex), so a LaTeX or
# Python run can drop artifacts here.
*.aux
*.fdb_latexmk
*.fls
*.synctex.gz
*.toc
*.out
*.log
ls-R
__pycache__/
*.pyc
